<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islamabad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Islamabad is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, a planned city built from the early 1960s at the foot of the Margalla Hills, next to Rawalpindi. Chosen under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayub-khan">Ayub Khan</a> to replace <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karachi">Karachi</a> as capital, it was laid out by the Greek planner Constantinos Doxiadis in sectors with green belts. It is home to the Faisal Mosque, one of the largest mosques in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islamabad.jpg" alt="Islamabad" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fassifarooq · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Faisal_Mosque,_Islamabad_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
